            <div xml:id="d240">

                <pb facs="0552" n="514" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v26/pg514"/>

                <head>240. Notes of Meeting<anchor n="1" xml:id="d240-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            from="1967-07-25T14:47:00-04:00" to="1967-07-25T15:47:00-04:00">July 25,
                            1967, 2:47–3:47 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Notes of the President’s Luncheon Meeting with Secretary
                        Rusk, Secretary McNamara, Walt
                        Rostow and George Christian, July 25, 1967, in the Mansion The
                    President read several memoranda which Secretary Rusk brought with him to the meeting.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d240-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>The President asked what this country was going to do about Indonesia. Mr.
                        Rostow said that a meeting would be
                    held on this problem tomorrow.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d240-f3"/> Secretary
                        Rusk said that $200 million was
                    planned within the consortium. Mr. Rostow
                    said Indonesia is going through a typical readjustment period. He said there was
                    a need for basic transportation and communication facilities. Secretary
                        Rusk then discussed <pb facs="0553"
                        n="515" xml:id="pg515"/> foreign assistance. He said the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi> Committee would be asked to
                    specify which countries it would eliminate if there is a cut back in foreign
                    assistance funds.</p>
                <p>[Here follows discussion unrelated to Indonesia.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
